"35a25c61-ba3b-5b21-8d90-ee3bc07b7267" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292609 #edb/ref 1074 "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{5y}{6}-2=0 & |\\,\\times 6 \\\\ 3x+y+6=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y-12=0 \\\\ 3x+y+6=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the second equation can easily be solved for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y+6 & =0 \\\\ y & =-3x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $y=-3x-6$ into the first equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y-12 & =0 \\\\ x+5(-3x-6)-12 & =0 \\\\ x-15x-30-12 & =0 \\\\ -14x-42 & =0 \\\\ -14x & =42 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $y,$ we substitute $x=-3$ into the equation $y=-3x-6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x-6 \\\\  & =-3(-3)-6 \\\\  & =9-6 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292696 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292696 #edb/ref 1069 "q-27009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292696 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292696 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$ \n\nI. The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nII. The function has a minimum value at  $x=2\\pi .$\n\nIII. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292696 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "69137884-05b3-53be-9c7c-95b53b1ed329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292696 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/9c/9c77bec4ebb04668fbff5176418ed9c09143a8660879fdf523a158c5f109006c.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=\\frac{\\pi 