592186045417] [17592186297238 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297238 #edb/ref 1069 "q-29608" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297238 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297238 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\nI. The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).$\n\nIII. The range of the function is $[-1,1].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297238 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c5a3a079-0ec8-5b33-84d2-568517288149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297238 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/31/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+2n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi +n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )=tan⁡(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=tan⁡x$ is $(-\\infty ,+\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297242 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297242 #edb/ref 1069 "q-29734" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297242 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297242 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x-9, & x<5 \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}-5, & x\\ge 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297242 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ee241ee-6c9b-581f-8e3e-00ecaf1e5967" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297242 #edb/ref 1074 "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}(x-9)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{10}(\\frac{x}{5}-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-9x)|}_{0}^{5}+{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-5x)|}_{5}^{10} \\\\  & =[\\frac{(5)^{2}}{2}-9(5)-\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2}+9(0)]+[\\frac{(10)^{2}}{10}-5(10)-\\frac{(5)^{2}}{10}+5(5)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{25}{2}-45]+[10-50-\\frac{25}{10}+25] \\\\  & =-50.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297244 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297244 #edb/ref 1069 "q-29742" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297244 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297244 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-9, & x<3 \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}-1, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297244 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "598039da-8879-5b3c-ab71-e359f8b00731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297244 #edb/ref 1074 "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(3x-9)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}(\\frac{x}{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}-9x)|}_{0}^{3}+{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-x)|}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3(3)^{2}}{2}-9(3)-\\frac{3(0)^{2}}{2}+9(0)]+[\\frac{(6)^{2}}{6}-6-\\frac{(3)^{2}}{6}+3] \\\\  & =[\\frac{27}{2}-27]+[6-6-\\frac{3}{2}+3] \\\\  & =-\\frac{27}{2}+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297633 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297633 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297633 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11c21c6d-1733-55e6-ae62-ff9455761bba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297779 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297779 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297779 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39ec9bc9-bb09-5cab-b8c8-16ed6e2d2ba1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186298244 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 1759